  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal obligations to West Virginia are $1.1B for FY2026 to date. The contracting picture shows 3,657 awards with an average award size of $308K. Obligations are down 40.0% year over year. Fiscal trends by year show a peak at $2B in FY24 and a decline to $1.9B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in the state, obligating $234M so far, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $213M and the Department of Justice with $200M. LEIDOS, INC. is the largest vendor by obligations at $105M, with SAWTOOTH CONSTRUCTION JV II LLC and IMPRES TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, INC following at $60.7M and $50.5M respectively. Other major industries by obligations are Other Computer Related Services at $157M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $137M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $122M, while Engineering Services accounts for $108M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending in West Virginia changed over recent years?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations rose from $1.5B in FY21 and FY22 to $1.7B in FY23 and $2B in FY24, then fell to $1.9B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26. Obligations are down 40.0% year over year. The current FY26 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Award volume is 3,657 with an average award size of $308K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drive federal contracting in West Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy leads buying with $234M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $213M and the Department of Justice at $200M. Other significant buyers include the Department of Defense at $142M and the Department of the Treasury at $134M. Industry concentrations include Other Computer Related Services at $157M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $137M."
      }
    ]
  },
